- Complete blood count (CBC) to assess for leukocytosis or left shift;  
- C-reactive protein (CRP) or procalcitonin to gauge infection severity and bacterial likelihood;  
- Chest X-ray (CXR) — essential to confirm pneumonia, atelectasis, effusion, or other pulmonary pathology;  
- Blood cultures — mandatory in postoperative febrile patients to rule out bacteremia/sepsis.  
Among these, CXR is the single most spatially informative test to localize and characterize the pulmonary abnormality suggested by symptoms and exam.

