- CXR confirms right lower lobe infiltrate (not wedge-shaped or peripheral like PE);  
- Absence of dyspnea, hemoptysis, or tachypnea argues strongly against PE;  
- Presence of productive cough, fever, chills, pleuritic pain, and crackles is classic for pneumonia;  
- Leukocytosis supports infection over embolism.  
